WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:02.907
- [Instructor] We are asked,
"How much time has passed

00:00:02.907 --> 00:00:05.597
"from the time on the
left," so right over here,

00:00:05.597 --> 00:00:07.000
"to the time on the right?"

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:07.960
Which we see right over here.

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:12.450
And they say that, "The time
passed is less than 12 hours."

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:14.630
So like always, pause this video

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:16.300
and see if you can answer that on your own

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:18.920
before we work on this together.

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:20.190
All right.

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:22.150
So first I just wanna figure out

00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:26.400
what time is being told by
each of these clock faces.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:27.920
So let's go here on the left.

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:31.120
So the first thing I'm gonna
do is look at the hour hand.

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:33.360
And we can see that the hour hand

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:36.190
has gone a little bit past six.

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:39.140
So it's going to be six-something.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:40.570
Six-something.

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:43.320
And then to figure out
what the minutes are

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:45.950
I can look at the minute
hand right over here.

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:50.460
And say, "Well, how far
has it gone in minutes?"

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:52.780
And I like to count by fives

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:56.180
because we know when we go
from 12 on the clock to one

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:58.120
that actually one, two, three,

00:00:58.120 --> 00:00:59.940
four, five minutes have gone by.

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:02.790
And in fact, between any two
numbers, it's five minutes.

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:07.430
So we go five, 10, 15, 20,

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:11.430
25, 30, 35, 40.

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:15.150
And then 41, 42, 43.

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:16.410
That's where it's pointing.

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:20.250
So it's 6:43, is where we're starting.

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:22.420
And then where we're ending, let's see.

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:25.240
The hour hand is a little bit past nine.

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:27.000
You can see it's past nine.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.220
And so it's not necessarily

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:30.160
what it's closest to, it's what it's past.

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:32.810
So even if the hour hand was like there,

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:36.470
even if it was closer to
10 but not quite at 10,

00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:38.650
you would say, "Okay, it's
gonna be nine-something."

00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:40.113
It's passed nine.

00:01:41.051 --> 00:01:42.940
And only if it got to 10 or past 10,

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:44.070
then you would say, "It's 10-something."

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:46.130
So this is gonna be nine-something.

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:47.950
And to figure out what that something is,

00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:50.710
once again, we start here,
we can count by fives.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:54.300
Five minutes, 10 minutes,
and then we have one more.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.250
We get to 11 minutes.

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:57.810
So it's 9:11.

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:00.610
And they tell us that this
is less than 12 hours apart.

00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:04.250
So it's not like 6:43 in
one day, maybe at night,

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:06.170
and then 9:11 the next morning.

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:09.150
This is maybe the same
morning or the same evening.

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:12.150
And so we can set up a timeline here.

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:13.970
So let's set up a timeline.

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:15.143
And so, let's see.

00:02:17.934 --> 00:02:19.840
The sixth hour is going to be important,

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:20.970
so that's six o'clock.

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:24.670
And let's see, maybe we wanna
go all the way to 10 o'clock.

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:27.040
So that we go beyond 9:11.

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:28.820
And so then we could say, let's go,

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:30.425
have to do seven, eight, and nine.

00:02:30.425 --> 00:02:32.160
I just wanna get my spacing right.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:36.360
So let's say that this is
seven o'clock right over here.

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:40.370
This is eight o'clock right over there.

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:43.570
And then that is nine
o'clock right over there.

00:02:43.570 --> 00:02:45.510
It's not gonna be a perfect drawing,

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:46.700
but this is pretty close.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:47.533
And so let's see.

00:02:47.533 --> 00:02:49.530
We are starting at 6:43.

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:53.000
Which is going to be, let's
see, it's going to be roughly,

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:54.380
and I just have to say roughly,

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:55.980
it's going to be right over there.

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:57.430
That's where we are starting.

00:02:57.430 --> 00:03:01.720
And then 9:11 is going to
be roughly right over there.

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:04.260
So that is when we are ending.

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:07.590
So how much time has gone by?

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:11.430
Well, to go from 6:43 to seven o'clock,

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:12.973
how many minutes is that?

00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:17.360
Well, to go from 43 minutes to 60 minutes,

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:19.460
you have to add 17 minutes.

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:24.410
So this right over here,
that is 17 minutes.

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:26.060
Just write it out.

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:29.340
And then we can see, we
have another two hours

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:32.120
that goes by from seven
o'clock to nine o'clock.

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:34.180
So then that's two hours.

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:37.610
And then to go from nine o'clock
to 9:11, what is going on?

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:40.190
Well, that's going to
be another 11 minutes.

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:42.630
11 minutes.

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:43.940
So how much time has happened?

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:48.030
It's going to be 17 minutes
plus two hours plus 11 minutes.

00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:49.100
Well, I find it a little bit easier

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:50.450
just to think about the minutes first.

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:55.450
So if I add 17 minutes to 11
minutes, 17 plus 11 is 28.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:00.720
I can do that on the side
if you want to see it.

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:02.350
Seven plus one is eight.

00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:04.310
One plus one is two.

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:08.810
So we are going to have a total
of two hours and 28 minutes.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:10.300
And I could write it that way.

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:15.300
Two hours, two hours and 28 minutes.

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:19.283
And we are done.

